    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d170-a1">

                <pb facs="0300" n="238" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg238"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 252.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Derby to Mr. Pierrepont</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1877-11-05"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 5,
                        1877</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your letter of the 10th
                    of September last, I have the honor to transmit herewith a copy of a letter
                    which I have received from the lords commissioners of Her Majesty’s treasury, on
                    the subject of the information that Mr. Eaton is desirous of obtaining,
                    respecting the civil service of the Crown.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>DERBY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwards Pierrepont</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
